*** Settings ***
Documentation     Bruno: IAM/User/User - Create. The first test saves the "user under
...               test" (${USER_ID}/${USER_ETAG}/${USER_EMAIL} globals) consumed by the
...               later suites and deleted last by 08_delete.robot.
Resource          resources/iam.resource
Suite Setup       Create Authorized API Session
Test Tags         iam    user    create


*** Test Cases ***
Create With Required Fields Succeeds
    ${email}=    Unique Email    robot.user
    ${name}=    Unique Display Name    Robot Test User
    ${resp}=    POST On Session    api    ${USER_API}
    ...    json=${{ {'display_name': $name, 'email': $email} }}
    ${id}    ${etag}=    Response Should Be Create Success    ${resp}
    Set Global Variable    ${USER_ID}    ${id}
    Set Global Variable    ${USER_ETAG}    ${etag}
    Set Global Variable    ${USER_EMAIL}    ${email}

Create With Readonly Fields Succeeds
    ${email}=    Unique Email    robot.readonly
    ${name}=    Unique Display Name    Robot Readonly User
    # Every key here except display_name/email is server-controlled, and the point of this
    # test is that the app SILENTLY DROPS them instead of erroring. 'is_owner' is the
    # subtle one: it is AutoGenerated() *and* Unique() ("only one owner per deployment"),
    # so if it ever reaches the unique check a second owner returns 400
    # common.err_unique_constraint_violated. Do not "fix" a failure here by removing
    # 'is_owner' from the payload - that hides the regression this test exists to catch.
    ${sent}=    Evaluate    {'id': '00000000000000000000000000', 'tenant_id': '00000000000000000000000000', 'display_name': $name, 'email': $email, 'is_owner': True, 'is_archived': '2026-03-24T10:54:50.610762Z', 'etag': '1775039846421692300'}
    ${resp}=    POST On Session    api    ${USER_API}    json=${sent}
    ${id}    ${etag}=    Response Should Be Create Success    ${resp}
    Set Suite Variable    ${READONLY_USER_ID}    ${id}
    Set Suite Variable    ${READONLY_SENT}    ${sent}

Get Ignores Readonly Fields
    ${resp}=    GET On Session    api    ${USER_API}/${READONLY_USER_ID}
    ${actual}=    Item Should Match Schema    ${resp}    ${IAM_SCHEMA_DIR}/user.json    200
    Should Be True    ${{ $actual.get('id') != $READONLY_SENT['id'] }}    msg=Readonly 'id' was not ignored
    Should Be True    ${{ $actual.get('tenant_id') != $READONLY_SENT['tenant_id'] }}    msg=Readonly 'tenant_id' was not ignored
    Should Be True    ${{ $actual.get('etag') != $READONLY_SENT['etag'] }}    msg=Readonly 'etag' was not ignored
    Should Be True    ${{ $actual.get('is_owner') != $READONLY_SENT['is_owner'] }}    msg=Readonly 'is_owner' was not ignored
    Should Be True    ${{ $actual.get('is_archived') != $READONLY_SENT['is_archived'] }}    msg=Readonly 'is_archived' was not ignored

